{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310654,"nonce":"S3MbhdQd4h4wAK3nYDtpf6ztEAQ=","title":"CHANNEL BUGS ALL CLOSED (matrix 22/22, 2026-07-13). Arc: lambda collapse 767806a0; uniform DynamicValue boxing; tryReceive class raw-box ...","message":"ROOT CAUSE (not channel, not thread, not bundle): anonymous closures named `\u003clambda_{counter}\u003e`\nwhere `lambda_counter` (hir_to_mir.rs:168) RESETS per lowering instance -\u003e every file's first\nclosure is `\u003clambda_0\u003e`. MIR keeps them distinct (fn33 Main vs fn660057 SpinPool) but the BACKEND\nBINDS BY NAME -\u003e two `\u003clambda_0\u003e` collapse. Adding rayzor.concurrent.Channel to a program that also\nuses SpinPool (RAYZOR_HAXE_MATMUL=1) made the streaming writer closure alias the pool worker-spawn\nclosure; Thread.spawn ran the wrong body/env -\u003e pool worker dispatched into rayzor_channel_receive,\nread pool control-block timestamp 0x1971234f as a channel handle -\u003e deterministic SIGBUS at gen\nstart. Same genus as vtable-thunk same-name collapse.\n\nFIX (767806a0): prefix lambda name with sanitized module name (hir_to_mir generate_lambda_skeleton)\n— same technique as __vtable_dispatch_thunk__\u003cqname\u003e. PLUS merge hardening: renumber re-keys\nexternal_function_names to renumbered ids (were left pre-renumber = detached name ground truth);\nimport merge PANICS on id slot with a different-named function (loud, not last-writer-wins silent).\nVerified: repro runs, standalone channel a-f pass, send_sync/debug_channel pass, server ok, 3-build\ndeterminism = 1 hash.\n\nDIAGNOSIS TECHNIQUE (reusable): RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR showed the SpinPool lambda's CALL was actually\ncoherent (targeted workerLoop) -\u003e misroute was at BACKEND symbol layer, not IR -\u003e spotted two\n`@\u003clambda_0\u003e` in the dump. Crash-PC-\u003efn-ptr-map named the faulting closure (id660057=SpinPool).\nRuntime eprintln in arc_get/channel_receive showed arc_get returned a timestamp as inner.\n\nRoot cause was a REPRESENTATION ASYMMETRY: Channel_send heap-boxed primitives (null-safety: a boxed\nint is non-null even at value 0, empty channel = 0 ptr) but stored class refs RAW; receive():T with a\nbare type param ERASES to I64, and the shared unbox's I64 arm reinterpreted the ptr bits as the int —\ncorrect for a raw class ptr, garbage (the box's heap address) for a boxed primitive. Explicit\n`new Channel\u003cInt\u003e(n)` worked (T=Int -\u003e I32 arm unboxes); only INFERRED `new Channel(n)`+primitive\nbroke. The naive \"unbox erased-I64 as int\" fix SIGSEGV'd inferred-CLASS (its receive also erases to\nI64; unboxing a raw class ptr corrupts). haxe_coerce_dynamic_to_int heuristic breaks Msg(0).\n\nTHE FIX (uniform representation, all Channel payloads become self-describing DynamicValues):\n- RUNTIME (type_system.rs): new `haxe_channel_unbox_erased(box_ptr)-\u003ei64` — null-\u003e0; tag ∈\n  {TYPE_INT,TYPE_FLOAT,TYPE_BOOL} -\u003e haxe_unbox_int(value); else -\u003e value_ptr as i64 (raw ref/string).\n  Non-heuristic. + 3 #[cfg(test)] unit tests incl the null-safety crux (boxed 0 is non-null != empty).\n- SEND (hir_to_mir `box_channel_payload`, modeled on maybe_box_value): refs -\u003e\n  haxe_box_reference_ptr(obj, REAL class id via value_ty.as_raw() — keeps Std.is/Type.typeof honest),\n  String -\u003e haxe_box_haxestring_ptr, prims -\u003e delegate to maybe_box_for_extern_call UNCHANGED.\n- RECEIVE (hir_to_mir `unbox_channel_return`, mirrors maybe_unbox_for_extern_return): only two arms\n  differ — I64 -\u003e haxe_channel_unbox_erased (fixes the bug); ref/`_` -\u003e haxe_unbox_reference_ptr\n  (refs boxed now, was raw passthrough). tryReceive Ptr(U8) nullable -\u003e passthrough (preserves\n  Null\u003cprim\u003e + `!= null`; empty 0 -\u003e null via null-guarded unbox fns).\n- DISPATCH FORKS (there is NO single chokepoint — CRITICAL): send gated at hir_to_mir 4 sites\n  (the \"EXTERN METHOD VAR\" is_mir_wrapper path ~13382 = the one concrete-channel primary, the\n  resolved-instance loop ~15298, the dynamic-receiver loop ~14765, Path-B ~16781); receive gated at\n  the 4 symmetric return sites (13520 primary after the Thread_join special-case, +14920/15460/16857).\n  Guard: mir_func_name/runtime_func == \"Channel_send\"/\"Channel_trySend\"/\"Channel_receive\"/\n  \"Channel_tryReceive\", arg i\u003e=1 on send (i==0 = channel handle, itself a ref — must NOT box).\n- CORRECTION to old note: Channel does NOT use the ptr_conversion_mask block (~15520); it's an\n  is_mir_wrapper path using the SHARED maybe_box_for_extern_call/maybe_unbox_for_extern_return.\n  Those shared BODIES are untouched (Arc/Mutex/Map/Thread.join/Deque.pop depend on them) — the fix is\n  purely at the gated call sites.\nVERIFIED: full chrepro matrix (Inferred 42|null; a/b/prim FIXED sum=100/recv 0..40; ClassPay*/c/e/f/d/\nprim2 stay green) + streaming StreamMsg (String+Bool round-trips) + 172-test run_haxe_tests.sh + 3\nruntime unit tests, all green. 6 self-asserting haxe tests added (2 proven to THROW pre-fix binary).\nKNOWN LIMITATION (pre-existing, NOT this fix): `var b:Int = ch.tryReceive()` leaves b BOXED (bare-Int\ntarget doesn't auto-unwrap Null\u003cT\u003e); use `.receive()` for bare values or `Null\u003cT\u003e` target + null-check.\nSame genus as the Null\u003cInt\u003e-\u003eInt cross-file assign bug. Inferred-FLOAT channel still lossy (erases to\nI64 -\u003e truncates); not in matrix, already broken pre-fix, out of scope.\n\nThe line-52 tryReceive \"Ptr(U8) nullable -\u003e passthrough\" was WRONG for CLASS payloads. `var n:StreamMsg\n= ch.tryReceive()` returned the raw DynamicValue BOX (not unboxed); then `n.text`/`n.done` field access\nread BOX memory (type_id/value_ptr) AS the class -\u003e garbage String ptr (const 0x19ab7562) -\u003e SIGSEGV in\n`haxe_string_concat_ptr` on the WRITER thread. This was the pre-existing ~50% crash in llama-chat's\noff-thread streaming writer coalesce loop (Main.hx `out += n.text`, feature 46806fd7). `receive()`\n(is_try=false) skipped the passthrough -\u003e `other` arm unboxes -\u003e always worked; only tryReceive broke.\nFIX (hir_to_mir.rs `unbox_channel_return`, is_try block): Void -\u003e keep raw passthrough (opaque);\nU8 (boxed ref: class/enum/anon/array erases to Ptr(U8)) -\u003e haxe_unbox_reference_ptr (null-guarded, so\nempty=null and `!= null` still work), mirroring the non-try `other` arm. VALIDATED: 62 llama-chat bundle\nruns 0 crash (was ~50%), output coherent, T2 receive\u003cclass\u003e + T4 INFERRED tryReceive\u003cclass\u003e green,\nno regression. **This crash poisoned every perf measurement this session (the 76\u003c-\u003e88 tok/s variance\nwas partly it) — always confirm crash-rate=0 before trusting A/B numbers on a streaming build.**\nSTILL BROKEN (separate pre-existing, NOT this fix, NOT regressed — T3 repro exit134 on old binary too):\nEXPLICIT `new Channel\u003cBox\u003e(n)` tryReceive\u003cclass\u003e resolves to concrete Ptr(Box) (not Ptr(U8)), takes the\n`other` arm / concrete send path, still returns garbage. llama-chat uses INFERRED channels so unaffected;\nthe explicit-param concrete path is a distinct unbox/send-asymmetry bug for a future session.\nRepro dir: /tmp/chanrepro (T2/T3/T4). Diagnosis: RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS crash-PC-\u003efn-ptr map named\n\u003clambda_main__0\u003e (the writer closure) as faulting; const fault addr =\u003e deterministic misread not UAF-churn.\n\nRoot cause (traced via new RAYZOR_TRACE_STDLIB_DISPATCH=1): the call DID route through the gated\nfork (EXTERN METHOD VAR -\u003e Channel_tryReceive) and unbox_channel_return DID run — but an explicit\n`Channel\u003cSomeClass\u003e` resolves the CONCRETE class, which converts to **Ptr(Void)** (not the erased\nPtr(U8)), and the is_try branch passed Void through RAW (my 490efb48 fix only covered U8). Caller\ngot the DynamicValue box -\u003e field access read box-as-class -\u003e garbage/SIGSEGV (T3: v=1961400480).\nFIX: is_try Void|U8 both unbox via haxe_unbox_reference_ptr (null-guarded). Blocking receive was\nnever affected (no passthrough). VERIFIED: T3 fixed (42/hello), T2/T4 unregressed, explicit-prim\nmatrix (T5) BYTE-IDENTICAL on pre-fix compiler (not a regression), llama-chat smoke coherent.\nNEW SEPARATE PRE-EXISTING BUG (T5, /tmp/chanrepro/T5.hx): explicit Channel\u003cInt\u003e.tryReceive into\nNull\u003cInt\u003e yields null for a REAL value (send(7) -\u003e \"int try: null\"); blocking receive fine. Same\non pre-fix compiler. Same genus as the known Null\u003cprim\u003e auto-unwrap limitation; needs its own MIR\ndump session (what does Null\u003cInt\u003e resolve to at that fork, and where does the value die).\nDEBUG TOOL: RAYZOR_TRACE_STDLIB_DISPATCH=1 prints class.method -\u003e runtime_func (instance/mir_wrapper)\nper stdlib dispatch at compile time — the tool that isolated this fork.\n\nUser directive: close ALL channel bugs. Matrix (/tmp/chanmatrix/Matrix.hx): {explicit,inferred} x\n{Int,Float,Bool,String,class} x {send/receive,trySend/tryReceive} + zero-values + empty + xthread\nclass payloads = 22/22 PASS. Fixed this pass: B5 explicit Null\u003cFloat\u003e tryReceive COMPILER PANIC\n(llvm FloatValue-vs-IntValue); B6/B8 Null\u003cprim\u003e tryReceive null/garbage; B7 explicit-class try\ngarbage in MULTI-instantiation programs; B9 inferred-float receive truncation 4.75-\u003e4; B10 static\ncounters (led to the two GENERAL statics bugs — see [[bugs_statics_lost_and_aliased_fixed]]).\nARCHITECTURE (the durable lesson): at the receive boundary static types CANNOT describe the payload\n(Ptr(U8)/Ptr(Void) = Null\u003cprim\u003e AND class; erased I64 = int AND float AND ref) -\u003e unboxing must be\nTAG-DRIVEN at runtime (haxe_channel_unbox_try: ref tags-\u003evalue_ptr, prim tags-\u003ekeep box, null-\u003enull)\nplus declared-type refinement (let_target_type_hint threads `var x:Float = ch.receive()` down to\npick the F64 arm; scoped non-try + floats). STILL OPEN (general, NOT channel): Null\u003cprim\u003e==literal\nnever unboxes (N1: plain `var x:Null\u003cInt\u003e=9; x==9` is false) — affects all Null\u003cprim\u003e compares.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_native_channel_spawned_receiver` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}